---
/* Retired sub-tab route, served as a STATIC HTML redirect artifact.
   See the sibling stub at /congress/leaders/ for why this is a 200 with a real
   document rather than an HTTP redirect: the published-path verification
   contract fetches every inventoried path with redirects disabled and treats
   an injected redirect response as a failure. */
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";

const target = "/congress/#momentum-section";
const description =
  "The Congress tickers view is now the ticker momentum section of the single /congress/ page — this page links to it.";
---

<Base
  title="Congress tickers — moved to /congress/ — Public Filings"
  description={description}
  active="congress"
  head={`<link rel="canonical" href="/congress/" /><meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url=${target}" />`}
>
  <main class="shell page">
    <div class="page-head">
      <div class="page-head-copy">
        <div class="kicker">/congress/tickers</div>
        <h1 class="page-title">This view moved</h1>
        <p class="page-lede">
          Ticker net disclosed flow is now the ticker momentum section that
          leads the single Congress page, where it can be read beside the
          disclosure feed and the member ranking without navigating between
          them. It also gained a 7d / 30d / 90d / 12m range control and a
          traded / filed basis toggle it did not have here.
        </p>
        <p class="page-lede">
          <a class="stub-link" href={target}>Go to ticker momentum →</a>
        </p>
        <div class="caveat-line">
          The target is <strong>not</strong> a like-for-like copy of this page, and
          saying so matters more than a reassuring sentence. This page windowed by
          trade date with a filing-date fallback; the section defaults to a
          <strong>trade-date</strong> basis, which excludes rows disclosing no trade
          date and states how many — switch the basis control to filing date to
          include them. It also renders a compact slice by default and expands on
          request. The interval arithmetic and the stated no-ticker count are
          unchanged, and the full published data remains at
          <a href="/congress/data/feed.v1.json">feed.v1.json</a>.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
